.\n$$\n\nThus, we have:\n\n- ${y}_{c}=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t+ϕ)$\n\n- ${y}_{c}=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2+ϕ)$\n\n- ${y}_{c}=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t$\n\nNext, we find the particular solution ${y}_{p}(t).$ Since the external force is a constant, we assume that the particular solution is also a constant,\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(t)=\\alpha .\n$$\n\nBy substituting the particular solution into the differential equation and equating coefficients, we find that $\\alpha =\\frac{1}{2}.$ So, the particular solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(t)=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nFinally, then, the general solution is given by the sum of the complementary and particular solutions. So, it can be written in any of the following forms:\n\n- ${y}_{c}=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t+ϕ)+\\frac{1}{2}$\n\n- ${y}_{c}=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t+ϕ)+\\frac{1}{2}$\n\n- ${y}_{c}=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t+\\frac{1}{2}$\n\nOnly II match the forms above. Therefore, the correct answer is \"II only\"." 13194139535478 true] [17592186351221 1000 #edb/ref 17592186351222 13194139535478 true] [17592186351221 1000 #edb/ref 17592186351223 13194139535478 true] [17592186351221 1000 #edb/ref 17592186351224 13194139535478 true] [17592186351221 1000 #edb/ref 17592186351225 13194139535478 true] [17592186351221 1000 #edb/ref 17592186351226 13194139535478 true] [17592186351221 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535478 true] [17592186351221 1041 "selection" 13194139535478 true] [17592186351221 1104 #edb/ref 17592186351226 13194139535478 true] [17592186351221 1110 #uuid "35b482fc-ca9a-58ce-9928-38400c619a62" 13194139535478 true] [17592186351222 1034 "II and III only" 13194139535478 true] [17592186351222 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535478 true] [17592186351222 1111 #uuid "a8b74756-4e38-5830-8a83-57d9fdf53c6a" 13194139535478 true] [17592186351223 1034 "I and III only" 13194139535478 true] [17592186351223 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535478 true] [17592186351223 1111 #uuid "2c02ece5-d65e-57fb