article is initially at the origin with zero velocity, find the position of the particle after $\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ seconds." 13194139535478 true] [17592186351262 1113 #uuid "1f3b61bf-2d9c-5a4f-b827-01f0e0d4bec0" 13194139535478 true] [17592186351262 1145 "The general solution to the equation of forced harmonic motion without damping is the sum of the complementary function and a particular solution.\n\nThe complementary solution ${y}_{c}$ represents simple harmonic motion and can be written as\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\omega t+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\omega t,\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ and $B$ are arbitrary constants of integration.\n\nIn our case,\n\n$$\n{\\omega }^{2}=49\\,⟹\\,\\omega =7.\n$$\n\nThus, we have\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡7t+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡7t.\n$$\n\nWe now need to find the particular integral ${y}_{p}(t).$\n\nThe external force is $-24\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.$ Therefore, we assume that the particular integral is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}=\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha ,\\beta $ are constants to be determined.\n\nSubstituting ${y}_{p}$ into the differential equation and equating coefficients gives $\\alpha =-\\frac{1}{2},\\beta =0.$\n\nTherefore, the particular solution ${y}_{p}(t)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(t)=-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\n$$\n\nand the general solution is\n\n$$\ny=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡7t+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡7t-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.\n$$\n\nSince the particle is initially at the origin with zero velocity, the initial conditions are $y(0)=0$ and ${y}^{′}(0)=0.$\n\nSolving with these conditions for $A$ and $B$ gives\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2},\\,B=0.\n$$\n\nSo our solution is\n\n$$\ny(t)=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡7t-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.\n$$\n\nTo find the position of the particle after $\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ seconds, we substitute into the equation $t=\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{2})-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=0\\,\\text{cm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535478 true] [17592186351263 1000 #edb/ref 17592186351264 13194139535478 true] [17592186351263 1000 #edb/ref 17592186351265 13194139535478 true] [17592186351263 1000 #edb/ref 17592186351266 13194139535478 true] [17592186351263 1000 #edb/ref 17592186351267 13194139535478 true] [17592186351263 1000 #edb/ref 17592186351268 13194139535478 true] [17592186351263 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535478 true] [17592186351263 1041 "selection" 13194139535478 true] [17592186351263 1104 #edb/ref 17592186351268 13194139535478 true] [17592186351263 1110 #uuid "7d7567ff-fa9e-5ccf-ae70-51ecef7ce9fa" 13194139535478 true] [17592186351264 1034 "y(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=1\\,\\text{cm}" 13194139535478 true] [17592186351264 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535478 true] [17592186351264 1111 #uuid "304d1e3b-0149-57d9-8e07-5540441f57a6" 13194139535478 true] [17592186351265 1034 "y(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=2\\,\\text{cm}" 13194139535478 true] [17592186351265 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535478 true] [17592186351265 1111 #uuid "16fcb282-3ad8-560d-9d3e-a9fdbe2f1b8b" 13194139535478 true] [17592186351266 1034 "y(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\,\\text{cm}" 13194139535478 true] [17592186351266 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535478 true] [17592186351266 1111 #uuid "653dc78d-776e-54c4-aba3-ad5f75074921" 13194139535478 true] [17592186351267 1034 "y(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{cm}" 13194139535478 true] [17592186351267 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535478 true] [17592186351267 1111 #uuid "9778b203-1c02-5bee-bfb4-ebeece72fcbe" 13194139535478 true] [17592186351268 1034 "y(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=0\\,\\text{cm}" 13194139535478 true] [17592186351268 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535478 true] [17592186351268 1111 #uuid "bc64d8c9-7b22-5819-88c0-04031bdad27a" 13194139535478 true] [17592186351269 1017 #edb/ref 17592186351270 13194139535478 true] [17592186351269 1089 "q-94376" 13194139535478 true] [17592186351269 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535478 true] [17592186351269 1100 "A particle is moving with forced harmonic motion without damping. The position of the particle $y(t)$ at time $t$ is governed by the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+y=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following could be used to represent the general solution for $y(t)?$\n\n- $y=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t+ϕ)-t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t$\n- $y=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t+ϕ)+2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t$\n- $y=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-2t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t$\n\nNote that $A,$ $B,$ $R$ and $ϕ$ are constants." 13194139535478 true] [17592186351269 1113 #uuid "09973ec5-6a1d-53be-934b-f8b7842cdc72" 13194139535478 true] [17592186351269 1145 "The general solution to this equation is the sum of the complementary function and a particular solution.\n\nFirst, we find the complementary solution ${y}_{c}(t),$ which is the solution to the simple harmonic motion equation ${y}^{″}+{\\omega }^{2}y=0.$\nIt can be written in three different forms:\n\n- ${y}_{c}=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\omega t+ϕ)$\n\n- ${y}_{c}=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\omega t+ϕ)$\n\n- ${y}_{c}=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\omega t+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\omega t$\n\nIn our case\n\n$$\n{\\omega }^{2}=1\\,⟹\\,\\omega =1.\n$$\n\nThus, we have:\n\n- ${y}_{c}=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t+ϕ)$\n\n- ${y}_{c}=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t+ϕ)$\n\n- ${y}_{c}=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡t$\n\nNext, we find the particular solution ${y}_{p}(t).$ The particular solution is of the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(t)=t(\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡t).\n$$\n\nBy substituting the particular solution into the differential equation and equating coefficients, we find that $\\alpha =-1$ and $\\beta =0.$ So, the particular solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(t)=-t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.\n$$\n\nFinally, then, the general solution is given by the sum of the complementary and particular solutions. So, it can be written in any of the following forms:\n\n- ${y}_{c}=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t+ϕ)-t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t$\n\n- ${y}_{c}=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t+ϕ)-t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t$\n\n- ${y}_{c}=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t$\n\nOnly I matches the forms above. Therefore, the correct answer is \"I only\"." 13194139535478 true] [17592186351270 1000 #edb/ref 17592186351271 13194139535478 true] [17592186351270 1000 #edb/ref 17592186351272 13194139535478 true] [17592186351270 1000 #edb/ref 17592186351273 13194139535478 true] [17592186351270 1000 #edb/ref 17592186351274 13194139535478 true] [17592186351270 1000 #edb/ref 17592186351275 13194139535478 true] [17592186351270 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535478 true] [17592186351270 1041 "selection" 13194139535478 true] [17592186351270 1104 #edb/ref 17592186351272 13194139535478 true] [17592186351270 1110 #uuid "bf8bb5ab-f082-597e-a99b-a10d9c4be09a" 13194139535478 true] [17592186351271 1034 "I and III only" 13194139535478 true] [17592186351271 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535478 true] [17592186351271 1111 #uuid "9b5421b9-92f6-5979-b02e-9712eac55210" 13194139535478 true] [17592186351272 1034 "I only" 13194139535478 true] [17592186351272 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535478 true] [17592186351272 1111 #uuid "51f9c8f0-ba85-598e-8cf4-0feac701abfb" 13194139535478 true] [17592186351273 1034 "III only" 13194139535478 true] [17592186351273 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535478 true] [17592186351273 1111 #uuid "2a653aa8-7afe-5016-add0-e4351110f4f4" 13194139535478 true] [17592186351274 1034 "I and II only" 13194139535478 true] [17592186351274 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535478 true] [17592186351274 1111 #uuid "a20eb1b7-408e-5a95-9e9d-1e4b80954d81" 13194139535478 true] [17592186351275 1034 "II only" 13194139535478 true] [17592186351275 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535478 true] [17592186351275 1111 #uuid "076b9728-e041-5716-ad89-2cfa6a0462fb" 13194139535478 true] [17592186351276 1017 #edb/ref 17592186351277 13194139535478 true] [17592186351276 1089 "q-94383" 13194139535478 true] [17592186351276 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535478 true] [17592186351276 1100 "A particle is moving with forced harmonic motion with damping. The position of the particle $y(t)$ at time $t$ is governed by the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+8{y}^{′}+41y=10{e}^{t}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following could be used to represent the general solution for $y(t)?$\n\n- $y={e}^{-4t}(A\\operatorname{cos}⁡5t+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡5t)+\\frac{{e}^{t}}{5}$\n- $y=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(9t+ϕ)+\\frac{{e}^{t}}{5}$\n- $y=R{e}^{-4t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t+ϕ)+10{e}^{t}$\n\nNote that $A,$ $B,$ $R$ and $ϕ$ are constants." 13194139535478 true] [17592186351276 1113 #uuid "e83ef381-2688-5e65-8917-dab31a31675d" 13194139535478 true] [17592186351276 1145 "The general solution is the sum of the complementary solution and the particular solution:\n\n$$\ny(t)={y}_{c}(t)+{y}_{p}(t)\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the complementary solution ${y}_{c}(t),$ which is the solution to the homogeneous equation ${y}^{″}+8{y}^{′}+41y=0.$ Writing down and solving the characteristic equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+8\\lambda +41 & =0 \\\\ ({\\lambda }^{2}+8\\lambda +16)-16+41 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +4)^{2}+25 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +4)^{2} & =-25 \\\\ \\lambda +4 & =\\pm 5\\text{i} \\\\ \\lambda  & =-4\\pm 5\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore the complementary function ${y}_{c}(t)$ can be expressed in any of the following forms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{c}(t) & ={e}^{-4t}(A\\operatorname{cos}⁡5t+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡5t), \\\\ {y}_{c}(t) & =R{e}^{-4t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t+ϕ), \\\\ {y}_{c}(t) & =R{e}^{-4t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t+ϕ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the particular solution ${y}_{p}(t).$ The particular solution is of the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(t)=\\alpha {e}^{t}.\n$$\n\nBy substituting the particular solution into the differential equation and equating coefficients, we find that $\\alpha =\\frac{1}{5}.$ So, the particular solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(t)=\\frac{{e}^{t}}{5}.\n$$\n\nFinally, then, the general solution is given by the sum of the complementary and particular solutions. So, it can be written in any of the following forms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(t) & ={e}^{-4t}(A\\operatorname{cos}⁡5t+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡5t)+\\frac{{e}^{t}}{5}, \\\\ y(t) & =R{e}^{-4t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t+ϕ)+\\frac{{e}^{t}}{5}, \\\\ y(t) & =R{e}^{-4t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t+ϕ)+\\frac{{e}^{t}}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOnly I matches the forms above. Therefore, the correct answer is \"I only\"." 13194139535478 true] [17592186351277 1000 #edb/ref 17592186351278 13194139535478 true] [17592186351277 1000 #edb/ref 17592186351279 13194139535478 true] [17592186351277 1000 #edb/ref 17592186351280 13194139535478 true] [17592186351277 1000 #edb/ref 17592186351281 13194139535478 true] [17592186351277 1000 #edb/ref 17592186351282 13194139535478 true] [17592186351277 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535478 true] [17592186351277 1041 "selection" 13194139535478 true] [17592186351277 1104 #edb/ref 17592186351279 13194139535478 true] [17592186351277 1110 #uuid "0b1cae30-f8b9-5ce6-ad58-43e95762085d" 13194139535478 true] [17592186351278 1034 "I and III only" 13194139535478 true] [17592186351278 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535478 true] [17592186351278 1111 #uuid "5d7fd9a1-349b-5b8e-8f71-4b17b56d5d2c" 13194139535478 true] [17592186351279 1034 "I only" 13194139535478 true] [17592186351279 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535478 true] [17592186351279 1111 #uuid "b2cb348c-0172-5197-961c-11cf29367f62" 13194139535478 true] [17592186351280 1034 "III only" 13194139535478 true] [17592186351280 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535478 true] [17592186351280 1111 #uuid "f2d59f86-dffc-588b-9b43-ee67ea32cf4f" 13194139535478 true] [17592186351281 1034 "I and II only" 13194139535478 true] [17592186351281 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535478 true] [1759218635